<Rive version="1" kind="fragment">

    <!-- =========================================================================
         NO NAME MAY OVERLAP A COLUMN — THE RULE FOR EVERY TEXT ON THIS PAGE.
         Any box holding text the MATCH casts — a seal's name, a side's name,
         anything whose length nobody chose — is `sizingValue="fixed"` with a
         width, `overflowValue="fitFontSize"` and `wrapValue="noWrap"`. It then
         shrinks its own font until the line fits and never crosses into what
         is beside it. `autoWidth` is the opposite of that: the box grows to
         whatever it was handed and runs straight through the next column, and
         a four-a-side roster of long names is a table of overlapping text.

         THE WIDTH IS THE GAP TO THE NEXT THING, minus a gutter. A seat's name
         starts at 150 and the first number column is centred at 340, so 165 is
         the name's, and the rest is the number's and the air between them.
         Move a column and move the width with it: nothing can check the pair,
         and a box that is too wide only shows up as a collision on a name long
         enough to reach.

         `noWrap` is not optional. With a fixed width and wrapping left on, a
         long name breaks onto a second line INSIDE a 26-high box rather than
         getting smaller — the fit then works on the wrapped block and the name
         comes out half-size and clipped instead of merely small.

         WHAT IS NOT FITTED: every label that comes from uiText.csv. Their
         length is decided by a brief rather than by a match, and a label that
         silently shrank would hide the fact that the line written for the slot
         is too long for it.
         =========================================================================

         =========================================================================
         STATS PAGE — the ledger after the whistle.
         Two tabs: the sides' totals, and the seats' own. Every word is bound, so
         uiText.csv keeps owning the copy; the literals here are lorem and exist
         only as what shows before the game pushes anything in.

         NO HEADING AND NO RESULT LINE. The page opened with "Match Stats" over
         a "Champion! / <side>" band, and both were saying what the two names
         and the two big numbers under them already said. What is left starts
         at the scoreline.
         ========================================================================= -->
    <Artboard viewModelId="3:30" viewModelInstanceId="3:59" defaultStateMachineId="2:211"
              x="500" y="0" width="900" height="880" styleId="2:220" name="Stats Page" id="0:3">

        <LayoutComponentStyle name="Style" id="2:220"/>

        <!-- ===================================================================
             PLAY AGAIN — folded into this page rather than sitting under it.
             It was a DOM panel at the centre of the screen and this card was
             mounted on top of it, so the prompt was behind the artboard and
             unreachable.

             ONE SELECTION, THREE INPUTS. `overCursor` is lit by whichever of
             the pad, the keyboard or the pointer moved last — the pointer
             writes it from these hover listeners, so a mouse and a D-pad can
             never disagree about which button is up. The click writes
             `overPick`, and systems/versus.js reads it on the frame it already
             polls the pads on.
             =================================================================== -->
